@@ -484,3 +484,119 @@
 When a prior is supplied, `association_prior_camera_mm` and
 `candidate_prior_distances_mm` preserve the exact camera-frame association input
 and distances for later diagnosis. No nearest-feature shortcut is applied.
+
+## Known-tube coped joint geometry
+
+`weldfinder.coped_joint` is a pure geometry API. It does not open a camera, register
+robot feedback, change calibration or send motion. All input profiles must already
+share the declared frame and millimetres. The recommended integrated convention
+is the frozen initial camera frame: AutoWeld transforms each stationary native
+acquisition into that frame and retains its measured transform/provenance.
+
+```python
+from weldfinder import fit_coped_joint, sample_coping_curve
+
+fit = fit_coped_joint(profiles, coordinate_frame='camera', radii_mm=(12.7, 12.7),
+                     joint_angle_deg=90., centerline_relation='compare')
+if fit['status'] == 'qualified':
+    curve = sample_coping_curve(fit['model'], actual_seam_seed_mm,
+                                coping_axis=0, span_deg=180., step_deg=1.)
+```
+
+`select_coped_surface_returns(cloud, *, min_run_points=12, max_scan_gap_px=3,
+max_jump_px=8)` selects native surface-fit support before registration/fitting.
+The native cloud must declare `units='mm'`, `coordinate_frame='camera'`, aligned
+finite `xyz_mm` (N×3) and nonnegative `uv` (N×2), with strictly increasing native
+pixel x. Up to 400,000 returns are supported. Consecutive x gaps greater than
+3 px or stripe-y jumps greater than 8 px start a new run; the default retains
+runs of at least 12 actual returns. Thresholds are explicit validated arguments.
+This rejects short disconnected glare islands using image-space evidence only,
+without testing a nominal tube fit, changing XYZ or bridging missing returns.
+
+It returns `{native_point_indices: [...], diagnostics: {...}}` plus a schema and
+`selected` / `no_supported_runs` status. Diagnostics retain the rule, parameters,
+input/selected/rejected counts and each run's original index span. Invalid units,
+frames, arrays or UV order raise errors. Empty valid clouds and clouds without a
+supported run return no indices. There is no invented seam, pose or surface.
+Callers preserve the **complete original native cloud and its hash**, record these
+indices/diagnostics, and subset both XYZ and membership hints only for cylinder
+surface fitting. Detection of the actual seam and angular coverage still uses
+its independently qualified native acquisition; this selection does not modify
+calibration or turn a predicted intersection into a measured return.
+
+Each profile is `{xyz_mm: ordered_Nx3, seam_point_mm: measured_root_in_common_frame,
+profile_id: unique_JSON_identity, provenance: opaque_JSON}`. Alternatively provide
+aligned `surface_labels` (0/1) or a common `seam_seed_mm` argument. Seed roots only
+bootstrap the two branches; robust mixture refinement recomputes membership from
+measured radial residuals. The returned `classification` aligns with every input
+return in concatenated original profile order: two radial residuals, surface label,
+inlier/ambiguous flags and profile index. No nominal cylinder return replaces a
+measurement. Per-surface support and all-point/inlier residual summaries are
+separate. Duplicate profile identities are rejected as repeated evidence.
+
+`fit_coped_joint(profiles, *, coordinate_frame='camera', radii_mm=(12.7,12.7),
+joint_angle_deg=90., seam_seed_mm=None, axis_hints=None,
+centerline_relation='compare')` accepts a known angle from 10 to 170 degrees.
+Orthogonality is exact at 90 degrees; other entered angles constrain the actual
+fit. Radii remain fixed. Three through 512 measured profiles and at most 400,000
+returns are supported. Nine PCA starts are checked for distinct competing axis
+solutions. At least 50 unambiguous inlier returns, 4 mm axial extent and 12 degrees
+angular support on each surface, adequate Jacobian rank, bounded residuals/outliers
+and whole-profile holdout validation are required. Missing seed support, scant
+views, ambiguous fits and unsupported intersections return `unobservable`,
+`ambiguous` or `rejected`, with `model=None` and explicit candidate diagnostics.
+`qualified` means these geometric gates passed; `accuracy_qualified` remains False.
+
+Default model selection compares intersecting centerlines (`d=0`, an explicit
+nominal assembly prior) with free skew centerlines. Both hypotheses remain under
+`model_comparison`. A free offset is selected only if whole-profile held-out radial
+RMS improves by at least `max(0.03 mm, 10%)` and three whole-profile deletion fits
+show a consistent nonzero offset. These deletion offsets and their scatter are
+conditional diagnostics, not a physical confidence interval. An insignificant
+extra offset must not manufacture missing angular intersection near a real crown.
+Callers can explicitly choose `centerline_relation='free'` or `'intersecting'`;
+selection and assumptions are recorded. No camera/laser/hand-eye rescaling occurs.
+
+A model has `axes=[{origin_mm,direction,radius_mm}, ...]`, `center_mm` (closest point
+on axis 0), `frame_rotation` columns `[a,e,n]`, `axis_offset_mm=d`, units/frame,
+`joint_angle_deg`, a content `model_id`, and `axis_role_ambiguous=True`. Axis 1 is
+`cos(beta)*a + sin(beta)*e`, through `center_mm + d*n`. Geometry alone cannot say
+which equal tube is the cut-ended branch. The caller must provide `coping_axis`
+using finite assembly/visible fixture evidence and retain that role assumption.
+
+`sample_coping_curve(model, seed_seam_mm, *, coping_axis=0, span_deg=180.,
+step_deg=1., direction_hint=None, root_sign=None)` selects one intersection root
+near an actual measured seam seed. It preserves the finite-root sign instead of
+switching roots at a crown. It returns predicted points, tangents, inward directions
+toward the selected tube centerline, centerline points, relative angles and explicit
+unresolved domain/cusp events. All points have `predicted_only=True`. A model
+prediction does not establish that a joint exists there. No real intersection
+returns a gap. Equal-radius crowns have no unique tangent: events include both
+one-sided tangents, including events between sampling nodes. A crown seed requires
+an explicit root sign/finite assembly interpretation; no normal-cross-product NaN
+or fabricated smooth tangent is accepted. `coverage_complete=False` and status
+`partial` keep these unresolved intervals visible to planning.
+
+`coping_reference_pose(model, seam_point_mm, *, coping_axis=0, standoff_mm=150.,
+tangent_hint=None)` returns a rigid 4x4 common-frame transform, translation in mm.
++Z points from the seam toward the selected coped tube centerline; origin lies
+150 mm outward by default, +Y follows the local tangent and +X completes the frame.
+A crown requires an explicitly supplied measured/one-sided tangent. It is a tool
+reference, not a measured physical torch installation or welding output.
+
+`project_coping_seam(model, measured_points_mm, seed_seam_mm, *, coping_axis=0,
+max_distance_mm=1., root_sign=None)` returns bounded association results with BOTH
+original `measured_point_mm` and separate `predicted_point_mm`, residual and angle.
+Remote points are not associated; originals are never replaced. AutoWeld owns
+local valley observation, view steering, continuous branch tracking, trajectory
+preflight, fresh capture timing, persistence, actual pose transforms and replay.
+
+## Cached native diagnostics
+
+`CalibrationCamera.native_diagnostics()` reads cached metadata under the existing
+pipeline lock without calling snapshot, camera SDK methods, controls or acquisition.
+It includes raw latest frame/observation/preview identities and ages, observation
+publication/analysis duration, raw point-cloud count/rejections/processing timings
+even when normal publication has expired, worker native thread IDs/alive status,
+queue lengths and lock wait. It returns no image bytes, arrays or XYZ coordinates.
+This is a diagnostic path only; it does not relax any downstream freshness gates.
